<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela bolivar softens to 477.50/478.50/dlr.</title>
<headline>Venezuela bolivar softens to 477.50/478.50/dlr.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan bolivar fell in heavy trade to 477.50/478.50 per dollar on strong demand for dollars from the interbank market, traders said.</p>
<p>On Friday the unit closed flat at 477.25/478.50 per dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;Demand was higher than normal, principally due to interbank demand,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>Brokers added Central Bank participation was only moderate. &quot;Because of that the dollar strengthened,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>((-- Silene Ramirez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
